  <item>
   <title>Chassidus: The Origins of Prayer ch. 1</title>
   <link>https://podcasters.spotify.com/pod/show/avrohom55</link>
   <itunes:author>Rabbi Bergstein</itunes:author>
   <description>&lt;p&gt;The Origins of Prayer ch. 1. Biblically, prayer is obligatory when in need; rabbinically each day. Kabbalistically, the Shema effects a greater divine consciousness in the spiritual cosmos (fuses Chochma and Bina). Shemoneh Esreh draws that consciousness into the emotional and practical realms (fuses the Midos (z”a) and Malchus).&lt;br&gt;Important caveats to Kabbalah study: physical descriptions are euphemism for spiritual realities; even divine names do not define the essence of G-d.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
   <guid isPermaLink="false">ceea472f-da4f-57e2-9077-1312686365b8</guid>
   <pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:13:00 +0000</pubDate>
   <enclosure url="https://anshei.nudeltech-torah.workers.dev/ep/2026-11-16-chassidus-the-origins-of-prayer-ch-1-ceea472f.mp3" length="8694165" type="audio/mpeg" />
