   <description>&lt;p&gt;An analogy for tzimtzum: a brilliant teacher seeking to transmit great ideas to a student, must first organize his/her thoughts and set aside the profound in favor of digestible building blocks. This scaffolding provides the student with the opportunity to ultimately reach the summit of the ideas.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
